BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2025 Opening Night Film & Party
DTSTART:20250516T020000Z
DTEND:20250516T051000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T020000Z
UID:kkOku708Mn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 180 mins (3h00m)\n\nDarren Thornton (SIFF 2017’s A
  Date for Mad Mary) writes and directs this humorous and tender Irish char
 mer about a gay YA novelist (James McArdle\, “Mare of Easttown”) who m
 ust look after four aging women left in his care. Writer Colin Thornton sc
 heduled to attend. Opening Night Tickets: $78 Members | $88 Non-MembersOpe
 ning Night VIP Tickets: $360 Members: Make sure to sign in to your SIFF a
 ccount before selecting tickets. Note: SIFF parties are for ages 21+\, and
  IDs will be checked at the door. No refunds will be issued for tickets pu
 rchased with an invalid ID.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/four-mothers
LOCATION:Paramount Theatre\, 911 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:April
DTSTART:20250516T193000Z
DTEND:20250516T215500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T193000Z
UID:TZvNdBwp6v
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 134 mins (2h14m)\n\nAn obstetrician who secretly pro
 vides abortions and other family planning services to a remote village in 
 Eastern Georgia finds herself thrust into the harsh\, investigative spotli
 ght when she loses a newborn while on duty in the unflinching second film 
 from Dea Kulumbegashvili (Beginning). Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/april\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Film Center (Sat 17 May\,
  8:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bitter Gold
DTSTART:20250516T200000Z
DTEND:20250516T213500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T200000Z
UID:gCY5lE7XDP
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nIn this pulse-pounding neo-wester
 n thriller set in the cutthroat artisanal mining industry in the deserts o
 f northern Chile\, 16-year-old Carola must take control of the family busi
 ness and stave off greedy\, gold-seeking rivals after her father gets seri
 ously injured.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/bitter-gold\n\nAlso playin
 g at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Thu 22 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beef
DTSTART:20250516T201500Z
DTEND:20250516T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T201500Z
UID:njeMQhcyUJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLati\, a first-generation Malian 
 migrant\, turns to rap to overcome the death of her father. Determined to 
 overcome her fears of performing and to confront her mom’s opposition\, 
 a new world opens up when she learns how to tap into her frustration and a
 nger to create empowering\, liberating rhymes. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/festival/beef\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown Hou
 se 1 (Thu 22 May\, 9:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Auction
DTSTART:20250516T203000Z
DTEND:20250516T221500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T203000Z
UID:11H3rYB1Gd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nWhen a long-lost painting\, stole
 n by the Nazis in 1939\, turns up in a cottage in Eastern France\, it sets
  in motion a story of intrigue\, deceit\, and surprise. Based on a remarka
 ble true story. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/auction\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Sun 18 May\, 5:15 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Build a Library
DTSTART:20250516T203000Z
DTEND:20250516T222000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T203000Z
UID:9lwfydGOfO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nWhen two local women set out to 
 decolonize Nairobi’s formerly whites-only McMillan Memorial Library and 
 turn it into a multicultural hub\, they must contend with their country’
 s history and a complicated web of bureaucracy over eight very long but re
 warding years. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/how-to-build
 -a-library\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Wed 21 M
 ay\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Manas
DTSTART:20250516T220000Z
DTEND:20250516T235500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T220000Z
UID:Qi0K2TjqQw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nSet in a corner of Brazil that r
 emains mostly untouched by the modern world\, this is an earnest and movi
 ng tale of Marcielle\, a young victim of abuse who yearns to find a way ou
 t of a hostile home and a village that has resisted change for generations
 . Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/manas\n\nAlso playing at:
 \n  • SIFF Film Center (Sun 18 May\, 7:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monk in Pieces
DTSTART:20250516T220000Z
DTEND:20250516T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T220000Z
UID:HrAR7Fy7U4
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nAs avant-garde multihyphenate gen
 ius Meredith Monk approaches her final project\, the immersive “Indra’
 s Net\,” she and her greatest protégés and collaborators relive and re
 interpret her storied career’s most enduring works. Director Billy Sheba
 r scheduled to attend. Attend the May 16 screening for a chance to win goo
 die bags from Hex Enduction Records & Books! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.
 siff.net/festival/monk-in-pieces\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Up
 town House 3 (Sat 17 May\, 9:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hanami
DTSTART:20250516T223000Z
DTEND:20250517T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T223000Z
UID:JnMi1IJW7G
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWeaving between the natural and m
 agical\, Nana lives on a remote volcanic island from where everybody leave
 s. Left by her mother soon after birth\, she will spend her life trying to
  find the right answer to the lingering question in her mind and soul: Sho
 uld she stay or should she go? Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/hanami\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Wed 21 M
 ay\, 9:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Under the Volcano
DTSTART:20250516T223000Z
DTEND:20250517T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T223000Z
UID:js05FSNh2G
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nA Ukrainian family on vacation i
 n the Canary Islands suddenly find themselves stranded upon Russia’s inv
 asion of their home country\, sending them into fits of desperation and in
 trospection as they wander the beaches speculating what comes next.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/under-the-volcano\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Sh
 oreline CC Theater (Tue 20 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blue Road: The Edna O'Brien Story
DTSTART:20250516T230000Z
DTEND:20250517T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T230000Z
UID:U7CdAtZx3f
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nThe controversial and boldly fem
 inist Irish author Edna O’Brien (“The Country Girls”) shares journal
  entries and provocative insight into her trailblazing career in a series 
 of late-in-life interviews in this Palm Springs International Film Festiva
 l award winner. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/blue-road-t
 he-edna-obrien-story\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1
  (Tue 20 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drowned Land
DTSTART:20250516T230000Z
DTEND:20250517T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T230000Z
UID:svw5VpCjPj
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nThe Choctaw Nation of southeaster
 n Oklahoma fights against cultural displacement and the developers who wis
 h to dam and divert the Kiamichi River\, one of the most ecologically dive
 rse bodies of water in the state\, in this call to action from SIFF 4th Wo
 rld Media Lab alum Colleen Thurston. Director Colleen Thurston\, cinematog
 rapher Charles Elmore\, and protagonist Charlotte Robbins scheduled to att
 end. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/drowned-land\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Tue 20 May\, 6:00 PM)\n\nFilm is a
 lso being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Billy
DTSTART:20250517T003000Z
DTEND:20250517T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T003000Z
UID:IsPpKCxmG7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nIn this compassionate yet distur
 bing documentary\, director Lawrence Côté-Collins inspects the life of f
 ormer filmmaking friend Billy Poulin\, now in prison for murder\, through 
 his own stockpile of video footage and deconstructs the effects of untreat
 ed schizophrenia. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/billy\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • SIFF Film Center (Sat 17 May\, 2:30 PM)\n\nFilm is
  also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
