BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250517T040000Z
DTEND:20250517T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T040000Z
UID:XRftCSEjdE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals. Before the screening\, stop by the lobby to explore merch and mater
 ials from Offbeat Films production company and learn more about their crea
 tive work. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/40-acres\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Wed 21 May\, 3:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chain Reactions
DTSTART:20250517T040000Z
DTEND:20250517T055500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T040000Z
UID:fKviLlmbRO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nFilm essayist and SIFF alum Alex
 andre O. Philippe (78/52\, Lynch/Oz) calls upon five horror luminaries—S
 tephen King and Takashi Miike among them—to discuss the impact 1974’s 
 seminal The Texas Chain Saw Massacre had upon their lives and careers. Di
 rector Alexandre Philippe scheduled to attend. Swap your leather face for 
 your thinking cap at the May 16 screening\, where BoneBat Comedy of Horror
 s Film Fest will be giving away goodies via trivia! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/festival/chain-reactions\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pa
 cific Place 11 (Sat 17 May\, 1:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Nature of Invisible Things
DTSTART:20250517T040000Z
DTEND:20250517T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T040000Z
UID:PyMFo8kFHF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nGloria and Sofia\, two 10-year-ol
 d girls\, meet during the summer holidays while spending the days in a hos
 pital. Gloria is accompanying her nurse mother and Sofia is visiting her g
 randmother with Alzheimer’s. Their playful and delicate bond will help t
 hem navigate the fragility of life. Director Rafaela Camelo scheduled to a
 ttend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-nature-of-invisi
 ble-things\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Sat 17 M
 ay\, 3:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
