SUMMARY:I Am Nevenka
DTSTART:20250521T200000Z
DTEND:20250521T220500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T200000Z
UID:ejwY3MthTk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nNevenka Fernández\, the town’
 s finance councilor\, is relentlessly pursued by the mayor\, a man used to
  always getting what he wants politically and personally. Nevenka decides 
 to report him\, turning her courageous fight into Spain’s first #MeToo c
 ase. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-am-nevenka\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Fri 23 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fly Me to the Moon
DTSTART:20250521T203000Z
DTEND:20250521T223500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T203000Z
UID:feY8hmNNWq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nIn Sasha Chuk’s autobiographic
 al coming-of-age drama\, young Yuen struggles to adapt to her new surround
 ings and social class when she and her mother emigrate from Mainland China
  to 1990s Hong Kong to reunite with the family patriarch. Sponsored by:\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/fly-me-to-the-moon\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • Shoreline CC Theater (Mon 19 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being stre
 amed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Khartoum
DTSTART:20250521T203000Z
DTEND:20250521T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T203000Z
UID:eZfFiux9CF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nThe Sudanese Civil War has displa
 ced over 10 million of its citizens. Now\, five survivors contend with the
 ir own memories\, and hope for a peaceful future\, using green screen tech
 nology to reenact their lives leading up to the military coup that forced 
 their evacuation. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/khartoum\
 n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Mon 19 May\, 9:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250521T220000Z
DTEND:20250522T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T220000Z
UID:7iAUDv91vh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals. Before the screening\, stop by the lobby to explore merch and mater
 ials from Offbeat Films production company and learn more about their crea
 tive work. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/40-acres\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Fri 16 May\, 9:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freeing Juanita
DTSTART:20250521T220000Z
DTEND:20250521T232500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T220000Z
UID:U84DCpkA19
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 74 mins (1h14m)\n\nAn Indigenous Maya Chuj couple ma
 ke a treacherous thousand-mile journey across Guatemala and into Mexico to
  demand the emancipation of their niece\, who was wrongfully imprisoned du
 ring her intended migration to the United States. Producer Tristan Call an
 d director's partner Caitlin Brzezinski scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:
 \n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/freeing-juanita\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Tue 20 May\, 5:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also bein
 g streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home Sweet Home
DTSTART:20250521T223000Z
DTEND:20250522T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T223000Z
UID:uFOvKJEWae
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nSingle mother Sofie starts a new
  career as a caretaker for the elderly\, only to be humbled by the toll it
  takes on her physical and mental state\, in this authentic and rewarding 
 glimpse at the uncelebrated world of healthcare workers from SIFF alum Fre
 lle Petersen. Director Frelle Petersen and actor Jette Søndergaard schedu
 led to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/home-sweet-h
 ome\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Tue 20 May\, 8:45 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monarch City
DTSTART:20250521T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T235000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T223000Z
UID:PgvphwmvxH
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nIn this soulful family drama shot
  in and around the Cascades\, a young adult in rural America must confront
  her family’s numerous hardships—addiction\, incarceration\, poverty
 —and find the grace in life’s most fragile moments. Director Titus Ric
 hard scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/m
 onarch-city\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Tue 20 
 May\, 6:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Doe
DTSTART:20250521T224500Z
DTEND:20250522T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T224500Z
UID:boGHR3eOBU
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nNearly 30 years after Gail aband
 oned her newborn son in the woods and returned to her conservative Christi
 an life\, the police came and arrested her for infanticide. From Tribeca-w
 inning documentarian Jessica Earnshaw (Hulu’s “Jacinta”). Director J
 essica Earnshaw and co-producer John Rudolf scheduled to attend. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/baby-doe\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • 
 AMC Pacific Place 11 (Tue 20 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:By Design
DTSTART:20250521T233000Z
DTEND:20250522T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T233000Z
UID:yXCe5NT3Pv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nPlayful provocateur Amanda Kramer
  (Please Baby Please\, SIFF 2024’s So Unreal) has crafted another audaci
 ous\, performance art-based piece of absurdist satire about fetish and des
 ire\, as a lonely woman (Juliette Lewis) swaps bodies with a chair\, only 
 to finally find comfort in life. Cast member Alisa Torres scheduled to att
 end. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/by-design\n\nAlso play
 ing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Tue 20 May\, 9:00 PM)\n\nFilm i
 s also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Village Next to Paradise
DTSTART:20250522T003000Z
DTEND:20250522T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T003000Z
UID:22oj8qOibX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 133 mins (2h13m)\n\nIn the first Somali film ever se
 lected for the Cannes Film Festival\, a villager and his sister are just t
 rying to make ends meet and send his son off to boarding school. But in a 
 world defined by chaos\, unease\, and civil unrest\, sometimes sacrifice i
 s the only answer. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-vill
 age-next-to-paradise\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Film Center (Mon 19 M
 ay\, 3:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sally
DTSTART:20250522T010000Z
DTEND:20250522T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T010000Z
UID:oFVv5AdarF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nAward-winning documentarian Cris
 tina Costantini directs this peek into the personal life of Sally Ride\, t
 he first American woman in space. But as Ride journeyed among the stars\, 
 she kept a nearly three-decade romance with author and tennis player Tam O
 ’Shaughnessy a secret. Before the May 22 screening\, stop by the Museum 
 of Flight’s table to learn about their upcoming Sally’s Day celebratio
 n in June. If you’re lucky\, you might even win a pair of museum passes.
  Sponsored by:        This film is also generously sponsored by the No
 vasio-Wilson Community Fund.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sally\n\nAls
 o playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Thu 22 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Suburban Fury
DTSTART:20250522T010000Z
DTEND:20250522T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T010000Z
UID:Tly2yaX25q
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nLocal documentarian Robinson Dev
 or (Zoo\, Pow Wow) returns to SIFF with this outré and probing biography 
 of Sara Jane Moore\, the FBI informant and single mother who tried to assa
 ssinate President Gerald Ford in 1975\, as told in her own words. Director
  Robinson Devor\, producer Jason Reid\, executive producer/head archivist 
 Bob Fink\, and co-producer Matt Levinthal scheduled to attend. RSVP to joi
 n Seattle Documentary Association for a happy hour celebrating local docum
 entary filmmaking at Sound Hotel directly before the film. Limited space a
 vailable. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/suburban-fury\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Fri 23 May\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
